    "900.4.10(256)": {"explanation": "RS exception 256: minimum lot frontage and lot area are whatever the lot had when By-law 569-2013 was enacted; at most two dwelling units per lot; minimum street setback of 7.5 m on Finch Ave., Brimley Rd. or Midland Ave., 6.0 m on Alexmuir Blvd., Cleadon Rd. or South Shields Ave., and 3.6 m on any other street; minimum 1.2 m side setback; maximum 40% lot coverage; a garage at least 0.3 m from an interior side lot line; and the lands must also comply with exception 900.4.10(336).", "code_refs": "none"},
    "900.4.10(99)": {"explanation": "RS exception 99: in all cases a 4.5 m minimum front setback, 1.5 m minimum setback from a street side lot line and 50% maximum lot coverage. A semi-detached house needs 12.0 m frontage and 371 m2 lot area for the whole building (0.3 m side setback), and 6.0 m and 185 m2 for each half; a detached house needs 6.0 m frontage and 185 m2 lot area. Certain named addresses on Robinson, August, Pharmacy, Albion and Madelaine Avenues are also governed by exceptions of former City of Scarborough by-law 9812, which we do not evaluate.", "code_refs": "none"},
